Static Testing – 
Testing project-related documents (reviews, walkthroughs, inspections).

Dynamic Testing – 
Testing the actual software (unit, integration, system, UAT).

🔑 Types of Testing
Unit Testing – Testing individual modules/components.
Integration Testing – Ensuring modules work together.
System Testing – End-to-end testing of the complete system.
UAT – Final validation by end-users before release.

Difference between QA and QC
– QA is process-oriented,
- QC is product-oriented.

Bug vs Defect
– Bug is found during testing, 
- defect is deviation from requirements.

Smoke vs Sanity Testing
Smoke = basic build verification, 
Sanity = narrow regression check.

Regression Testing 
Ensures new changes don’t break existing functionality.

Functional vs Non-Functional Testing 
Functional = features,
Non-functional = performance,
security, usability.

Agile Testing – Continuous testing in iterative sprints.

Test Plan vs Test Strategy – 
Plan = project-specific,
Strategy = organization-level approach.
